      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-16150",
      ":question/problem": "The functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are differentiable on an open interval containing $x =-3$. The values of $f$, $g$, and their respective derivatives are shown in the following table:\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $f^{\u2032}(x)$ | $g(x)$ | $g^{\u2032}(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $-3$ | $0$ | $7$ | $-3$ | $0$ |\n\nFind $lim_(x \u2192 - 3)(f(x))/(x - g(x))$."
